    "type": "reasoning",
    "text": "Row 8 (n=33): sop issues:\n- \"not only for the diagram...\" — \"not\" held in `discourse` of c2! That's L2: \"A word with content is held in `discourse`, so its place in the sentence is lost.\" Indeed \"not\" is a negation word placed in discourse → L2. Yes, clear violation: \"not\" should be `negation` (of the clause or of the \"only\" phrase). L2.\n\nAlso \"on\" as modifier (from \"from now on\" split) and \"only\" modifier. The main defect: \"not\" in discourse → L2.\n\nCorrected circuit: take from alt? Alt has \"negation=no\" on c2 with modifier \"matter\" and treats \"no matter which\" wrongly, so no. I'll write my own based on sop with \"not\" as negation.\n\nActually I should double-check \"not only\" — \"not\" negates \"only\"? Schema: negation holds negation words. Put negation=\"not\" on c2. Good.\n\nCorrected: \n@c1 declarative verb want subject n1; relation \"to\" c1→c2; c2 nonfinite verb be subject n2 complement n3 modifier \"only\" negation \"not\" ... plus relations.\n\nLet me write:\n@n1 syntax.nominal head=\"I\"\n@c1 syntax.clause form=declarative verb=\"want\" subject=$n1\n@n2 syntax.nominal dependent=\"my\" head=\"avatar\"\n@r1 syntax.relation marker=\"to\" from=$c1 to=$c2\n@c2 syntax.clause form=nonfinite verb=\"be\" negation=\"not\" modifier=\"only\" modifier=\"on\" subject=$n2 complement=$n3\n@n3 syntax.nominal dependent=\"a\" dependent=\"male\" head=\"figure\"\n@r2 syntax.relation marker=\"for\" from=$c2 to=$n4\n@n4 syntax.nominal dependent=\"every\" head=\"session\"\n@r3 syntax.relation marker=\"from\" from=$c2 to=$n5\n@n5 syntax.nominal head=\"now\"\n@r4 syntax.relation marker=\"for\" from=$c2 to=$n6\n@n6 syntax.nominal dependent=\"the\" head=\"diagram\"\n@n7 syntax.nominal head=\"I\"\n@c3 syntax.clause form=declarative verb=\"have\" modifier=\"open\" modifier=\"right\" modifier=\"now\" subject=$n7\n@r5 syntax.relation from=$n6 to=$c3\n\nRow 9 (n=35): \"Whatever else changes on the page, my avatar should stay a man figure until I tell you otherwise.\"\nSOP: n1 nominal head \"Whatever\" dependent \"else\"; c1 declarative verb \"changes\" subject n1; r1 marker on from c1 to n2 (the page); c2 auxiliary should verb stay subject n3 complement n4; r2 marker until from c2 to c3; c3 declarative verb tell modifier \"otherwise\" subject n5 complement n6; r3 from c2 to c1.\n\nIs r3 (relation from c2 to c1) acceptable — ties the subordinate clause \"Whatever else changes on the page\" to the main clause. Yes, that's a valid tie. \n\n\"Whatever else\" — nominal with head \"Whatever\", dependent \"else\": per settled case \"everything else\" one nominal with \"else\" dependent. Fine.\n\n\"otherwise\" as modifier of clause \"tell\" — modifier is for words neither nominal nor marker; fine.\n\n\"tell you otherwise\" — c3 has complement n6 \"you\" and \"otherwise\" modifier. OK.\n\nL8 for row 9.\n\nRow 10 (n=36): \"If you can, set my avatar to the male option and keep it for the next time I open the app on this machine.\"\nSOP: r1 marker \"If\" from c2 to c1 — relation starts at c2 (the imperative \"set\") and ends at c1 (\"you can\"). Hmm, the rule: \"The start of a relation with a marker: the clause, or any nominal of that clause that grammar allows\". \"If\" here heads the clause \"if you can\" which precedes... Actually relation from=$c2 to=$c1 means relation marker \"If\" from the main clause to the subordinate clause. Settled case: \"A clause that ends a relation with a marker stands inside the clause where the relation starts.\" So c1 (\"you can\") stands inside c2 — correct: the imperative is c2, and \"if you can\" is subordinate. Start at c2 = the clause. Passes.\n\nc1: declarative verb \"can\" subject n1 — elliptical tag clause with auxiliary as verb: allowed (\"would you\", \"if you can\").\n\nc2 imperative set complement n2; r2 to n3; k1 coordination conjunct c2, c3 (keep) — fine. c3 imperative keep complement n4 (\"it\"); r3 for → n5 \"the next time\"; c4 declarative open subject n6 complement n7; r4 marker \"on\" from c4 to n8 (this machine) attachment ambiguous; r5 from n5 to c4.\n\n\"the next time I open the app on this machine\" — n5 \"time\" tied to c4 by r5. Fine.\n\nImportant: \"keep it for the next time...\" — complement n4 \"it\". Fine.\n\nL8 for row 10.\n\nNow rows 11-13 (n=37, 38, 40), then 14 (n=41) I have partially. Let me dump 11-14 text+sop.\n\nAlso I need to produce corrections for rejections. Fine.\n\nLet me proceed with dumps of 3-4 rows each. That's ~40 more calls for 150 rows... too many. Let me use 5 rows per dump (~text+sop ≈ 5*900 = 4.5KB) — comfortable. 150/5 = 30 calls. Still many but acceptable? Each call is cheap in tokens. Let's use 6 rows per dump (~5.5KB).\n\nActually earlier 10 rows text+sop+alt = 17.8KB, so text+sop ≈ 12KB for 10 → 6 rows ≈ 7KB. Good, 6 per dump → 25 dumps.\n\nLet's go: 11-16.",
