    "text": "Now assemble and check: 17 + 66 + 67 = 150. Verify the n set matches the CSV exactly and each line valid JSON.\n\nThen sanity check: should I revisit a few borderline rows to increase discrimination? Let me review the distribution: 4 rejections (33, 101, 165, 349). Hmm. Let me do a second pass over rows where sop and alt differ substantively — those are the ones where one formalizer deviated, more likely to be judged wrong. I can diff sop vs alt quickly by printing rows where they differ beyond trivial things. Actually, from what I read, alt frequently differed (e.g., n=24 alt wrong, n=31 alt wrong with \"am\" auxiliary, n=54 alt fine, n=349 alt?). The sop seems to be from the better formalizer overall, so few rejections is plausible.\n\nBut let me double check a handful of rows where the sop looked slightly off that I may have waved through:\n\n1. n=28 (row 5) \"Keep it as a male figure from here on.\" — modifier \"on\" of c1 AND relation \"from\"→\"here\". Actually wait: is \"on\" attached, and \"here\"? \"from here on\": relation \"from\" from c1 to \"here\", plus \"on\" modifier. OK.\n\n2. n=35 (row 9): r3 from c2 to c1 — relation with no marker from the main clause to the subordinate. Fine.\n\n3. n=43 (row 43/n=108): \"Whatever I do in the diagram tab\" — r1 marker \"Whatever\" from c2 to c1. \"Whatever\" is a question word/relativizer; as a marker of the relation starting at c2. Fine.\n\n4. n=56 (row 22): k1 \"then\" joins c1 c2; fine.\n\n5. n=59 (row 24): \"for today\" relation from c2 to n5 \"today\" — \"today\" as a nominal head; fine.\n\n6. n=72 (row 72, n=185): \"Use an old man for the avatar from now on.\" — r2 \"from\" from c1 to n3 \"now\", and \"on\" as modifier. Fine.\n\n7. n=100 (row 31): \"The avatar I use should be the woman.\" L8.\n\n8. n=102 (row 38): fine.\n\n9. n=165 rejected; n=98 accepted (k1 \"not only\" coordination) — inconsistency! n=98 (row 34) and n=142 (row 142, n=346) use k1 coordination with conjunction \"not only\" joining r2 and r4 → I passed. n=33/n=165 have \"not\" in discourse → L2. That's consistent: same message, different circuits, both readings judged by their own merit. Good. Actually wait, is the \"not only\" coordination also a \"negation word held in another place\" (L1)? I decided no. Hmm, let me reconsider once: L1 criterion: \"An `auxiliary` or `negation` word is held in another place, or negates the wrong clause.\" In row 34, \"not\" stands in the coordination's `conjunction` field (\"not only\"), so it is held in another place than `negation`... \n\nHmm. If I grade n=98/n=346 as L1, then only n=33/n=165 (discourse) would be L2 — a similar but different placement. Strictly, L1's clause says \"An auxiliary or negation word is held in another place, or negates the wrong clause.\" The coordination's conjunction field holding \"not only\" — \"not\" IS in another place. But it doesn't negate the wrong clause; it qualifies the second conjunct's relation. Semantically the message's \"not only for the diagram\" is exactly \"the second for-phrase is not exclusive\", which a coordination with \"not only\" conveys.\n\nThe intent of L1 there is about auxiliaries and negations being misplaced so that the clause's polarity is wrong. In row 34 the polarity reading is preserved. I'll keep L8 for those — and my rejections for 33/165 rest on L2's explicit wording (discourse → place lost), which is a cleaner rule.\n\nAlright. One more consideration: 4 rejections in 150 might be low but the judging instructions emphasize fairness and accepting plausible readings. There are also legitimate variations the rules explicitly bless. I'm comfortable, though let me re-scan a few more of the 0-82 rows that I judged quickly in bulk (rows 53-82 were nearly all copy-paste of earlier patterns that I checked). I did look at each. Fine.\n\nLet me also double-check row 128 (n=319) and row 149 (n=353) final decision: L8 (passed). And n=311 L8.\n\nNow assemble the file: cat p1 p2 p3 > objects-01-advanced.p01.verdicts.jsonl. Then validate JSON, count 150, and confirm the n values match CSV order/set.\n\nAlso: I must double check the notes requirement — for rejections, quote the words in single quotes and name the wrong statement. My notes:\n- n=33: \"'not' in 'not only for the diagram I have open right now' is held in 'discourse', so its place...\" — wait, I wrote for n=33: \"'not' in 'not only for the diagram I have open right now' is held in 'discourse', so the negation of the second 'for' phrase is lost.\" Good, quotes present.\n- n=101: quotes 'figure', 'make a woman figure my avatar'. Good.\n- n=165: quotes 'not' and phrase. Good.\n- n=349: quotes 'my avatar', 'the robot but painted blue my avatar'. Good.\n\nLet me assemble and validate.",
